{"sentences": [{"sentence_id": "s1", "sentence": "Thirty-one trials have tested α4-integrin blockade in multiple sclerosis, with Biogen as the lead sponsor in 26 of them.", "cites": ["NCT05265728"]}, {"sentence_id": "s2", "sentence": "Nine trials were terminated, including a Phase 3 study (NCT01416181) that did not achieve statistical significance on primary or secondary endpoints.", "cites": ["NCT01416181"]}, {"sentence_id": "s3", "sentence": "Natalizumab is approved for relapsing forms of multiple sclerosis and acts by blocking α4-integrin to inhibit lymphocyte trafficking into the central nervous system.", "cites": ["FDA:c5fdde91-1989-4dd2-9129-4f3323ea2962"]}, {"sentence_id": "s4", "sentence": "Natalizumab carries a FDA boxed warning for progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy (PML), a risk that increases with anti-JCV antibody status, treatment duration, and prior immunosuppressant use.", "cites": ["FDA:c5fdde91-1989-4dd2-9129-4f3323ea2962"]}, {"sentence_id": "s5", "sentence": "The risk of PML has led to restricted access via the TOUCH Prescribing Program, which limits broader use despite efficacy.", "cites": ["FDA:c5fdde91-1989-4dd2-9129-4f3323ea2962"]}, {"sentence_id": "s6", "sentence": "No other drugs in the α4-integrin inhibitor class have been approved for multiple sclerosis.", "cites": ["FDA:c5fdde91-1989-4dd2-9129-4f3323ea2962"]}, {"sentence_id": "s7", "sentence": "Recent observational data suggest that extended interval dosing of natalizumab may lead to low drug trough levels and emergence of neutralizing anti-drug antibodies, risking loss of efficacy.", "cites": ["PMID:42969026"]}, {"sentence_id": "s8", "sentence": "Lack of expected lymphocytosis on treatment may serve as a biomarker for anti-drug antibody development.", "cites": ["PMID:42891510"]}, {"sentence_id": "s9", "sentence": "Natalizumab may exacerbate neuromyelitis optica spectrum disorder due to blockade of endothelial VCAM1-astrocytic integrin α4 interaction.", "cites": ["PMID:41671178"]}, {"sentence_id": "s10", "sentence": "Despite high efficacy, the PML risk profile places natalizumab at a competitive disadvantage compared to newer agents with more favorable safety profiles.", "cites": ["FDA:c5fdde91-1989-4dd2-9129-4f3323ea2962"]}], "sources": [{"id": "NCT05265728", "text": "{"nct":"NCT05265728","title":"A Study to Evaluate Efficacy, Safety, Pharmacokinetics, and Pharmacodynamics of Multiple Doses of N…","state":"stopped","drug":"natalizumab","start_year":2022,"end_year":2024,"phase":"3","overall_status":"TERMINATED","why_stopped":"Due to sponsor decision, not for efficacy or safety reasons.","lead_sponsor":"Biogen"}
